  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 125 PM Sunday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Below normal temperatures to start the week, \ngradually moderate through the end of the week.\n\nAt the surface, a 1033 mb Canadian high over the Midwest today will \nslowly migrate eastward across the OH Valley and mid-Atlantic \nthrough mid-week, then remain in place and moderate through the end \nof the week. Aloft, the positively tilted longwave trough will \nremain over the eastern US today and Monday, while a s/w tracks \nacross the Deep South/Southeast US and offshore. The trough will \nthen shift ewd and offshore, with the sub-tropical ridge, which \nshould amplify to the west Mon and Tue, tilting to the east and \nextending across the area Wed-Fri. \n\nBelow to well below normal temperatures will continue through Mon \nnight. Near to below freezing low temperatures are expected across \nmuch of central NC through mid-week, though the urban areas and \nportions of the Sandhills and Coastal Plain may creep above freezing \nby Thu morning. Monday night should be the coldest, with lows in the \nmid 20s to low 30s, but as noted previously the growing season has \nended and thus frost/freeze products will not be issued. High \ntemperatures should gradually moderate through the week, with near \nto above normal highs expected from Tue (low to mid 60s) to Sat and \nSun (upr 60s to low 70s). Dry weather is expected to prevail through \nat least Fri night.",
